always-delete regression, workflow-lint) and never names this pre-existing test as a consumer to update."],"finding":"The plan changes run_access_check's JQL-retry loop (raising JQL_RETRY_COUNT and swapping fixed JQL_RETRY_SLEEP for exponential backoff) but its test/consumer inventory omits the existing regression test tests/scripts/bridge/test_jira_capability_probe.py::test_probe_retries_jql_search_three_times, which hard-pins the old schedule via `search_issues.call_count == 6` and `delays == [5, 5, 5, 5, 5]`.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f591e50e573c7f9fc","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 1 and Testing section (\"extract the JQL-search retry into a small helper ... Raise the default budget ... sleeps with exponential backoff\")","norm_id":"ne051b98196f47675","priority":0.85,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["tests/scripts/bridge/test_jira_capability_probe.py::test_probe_retries_jql_search_three_times: its `call_count == 6` assertion breaks the moment the default JQL_RETRY_COUNT is raised, and its `delays == [5, 5, 5, 5, 5]` assertion breaks the moment fixed sleeps become exponential backoff — leaving a suite-red test the plan did not schedule for update."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add the existing test to the Testing/scope inventory and specify how it will be updated (assert the new backoff schedule and new default count, or reparametrize against the module constants rather than literals).","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","vague/subjective terms present: robust"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the concrete default JIRA_PROBE_JQL_RETRIES, JIRA_PROBE_JQL_SLEEP, and backoff cap values (and the observed REB lag they must cover) in the plan.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3022,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Raise the default budget to cover observed REB lag'","'base * 2**attempt, capped' — cap value unstated","'a safe default that covers observed REB lag' — the observed lag is never quantified"],"finding":"The plan mandates 'raise the default budget to cover observed REB lag' with a 'capped' exponential backoff, but never states the concrete default retry count, base sleep, or cap value — nor the observed REB lag figure the default must cover. The executor must invent these numbers.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb0f24873e3d831ca","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 1 / Outcome 1 / AC line 1","norm_id":"n5aef97720e49b22a","priority":0.2978,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor picks a default too short and the Cloud lane still flakes","Two implementers choose different defaults/caps"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add explicit numbers, e.g. 'default retries 8, base sleep 5s, cap 40s per attempt (~total >2min), covering the observed REB index lag of ~Ns'.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5556,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Scope the failure/cancel teardown sweep to the run's UNIQUE label (or a per-run/per-commit token), not the shared `rebar-id:` prefix, so concurrent runs cannot delete each other's in-flight probe issues.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9","T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Outcome 2(c): 'on failure/cancel runs a label-sweep teardown backstop that deletes any leaked `rebar-id:` probe issue'","Plan step 2: 'teardown step that lists+deletes leftover `labels ~ \"rebar-id:\"` issues'","The probe itself is described as creating a 'uniquely-labeled throwaway issue' — the sweep uses the shared prefix, not that unique label"],"finding":"The failure/cancel label-sweep teardown deletes ALL issues matching the shared prefix `labels ~ \"rebar-id:\"`, not the run-unique label the probe creates. If two probe runs (or a probe run and any other rebar operation that labels an issue with a rebar-id) execute concurrently against the live REB project, one run's teardown can delete another run's in-flight probe issue (or a legitimately-in-use issue), a check-then-act blast-radius hazard on shared external state.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f915f71ddcfd5d35f","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 2 / Outcome 2(c): 'label-sweep teardown backstop that deletes any leaked `rebar-id:` probe issue'","norm_id":"n3e7a7c2983a13b9d","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two dispatched Live External Integration runs overlap against the same REB project; run A fails and its teardown sweeps run B's still-in-flight probe issue, causing run B's by-key operations to fail or a spurious delete of an unrelated rebar-labeled issue"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Have the probe/lane derive a run-unique label token (e.g. `rebar-probe-run:<run_id>`) and make the teardown sweep match only that token; document that the shared-prefix sweep is unsafe under concurrency.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Consider Atlassian's `reconcileIssues` parameter on the enhanced JQL search endpoint (POST /rest/api/3/search/jql) as the read-after-write remedy for the STEP_JQL_SEARCH lag, and either adopt it (passing the probe's issue_key) or record why the backoff-retry workaround is preferred (e.g. AcliClient.search_issues does not target the enhanced endpoint).","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'the retry budget is a fixed JQL_RETRY_COUNT=6 x JQL_RETRY_SLEEP=5s with no backoff, which is shorter than Jira Cloud's search-index eventual-consistency lag'","Retrieved (developer.atlassian.com, REST v3 issue-search): 'Recent updates might not be immediately visible... If you need read-after-write consistency, you can utilize the reconcileIssues parameter to ensure stronger consistency assurances.'","Retrieved (Atlassian community): 'the enhanced JQL Search API supports the reconcileIssues parameter, which ensures consistent results for the specified issue IDs (up to 50 issues).'","Probe already holds the created issue_key (access_check.py L153) — the exact input reconcileIssues wants — so the deterministic path is available, not a longer poll.","ABSENCE: the plan never names reconcileIssues / Search-and-Reconcile, so a reviewer cannot tell whether it was rejected for a reason (e.g. AcliClient's search_issues may not target the enhanced endpoint) or simply unconsidered."],"finding":"The plan root-causes the STEP_JQL_SEARCH flake as Jira Cloud search-index eventual-consistency lag and remedies it with a longer retry budget + exponential backoff, but does not consider Atlassian's first-party read-after-write remedy for exactly this problem: the `reconcileIssues` parameter on the enhanced JQL search endpoint (POST /rest/api/3/search/jql), which returns consistent results for specified issue IDs (up to 50).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4258a76676b1fdcc","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Outcome item 1 / Plan step 1 / AC line 1 ('exponential backoff and raise the budget')","norm_id":"n3d6ec510e57f9216","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A backoff budget tuned to 'observed REB lag' still flakes when Cloud index lag exceeds the raised default under load — a race the retry approach can never fully close, whereas reconcileIssues is designed to be deterministic.","CI operators forced to keep bumping JIRA_PROBE_JQL_RETRIES/SLEEP because the underlying non-determinism was worked around, not removed."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"In Plan step 1 / Context, add a note evaluating reconcileIssues: since the probe already has issue_key, prefer a reconcileIssues-scoped search for deterministic read-after-write, falling back to the backoff-retry loop only if the client's search path cannot target POST /rest/api/3/search/jql; document the chosen path and its reason.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiab